---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import { readRepoFile, REPO, processTasks, processCampaign, PROCESS_PILOT } from "@/lib/data";
import { renderMarkdown } from "@/lib/markdown";
const inventory = processTasks();
const pilot = processCampaign(PROCESS_PILOT);
const base = `${REPO}/blob/main/docs/process/`;
// The three documents render on one page, so links between them become anchors. The worked example in tasks.md
// spells out a task's planted cases; like the desk traps it stays in the repository.
const tasksMd = readRepoFile("docs/process/tasks.md");
const cut = tasksMd.indexOf("\n## 4. Worked example");
const tasksPart = (cut > 0 ? tasksMd.slice(0, cut) : tasksMd) +
  `\n\nThe worked example, which walks through \`procure-to-pay-week\` turn by turn with its planted cases, is in [the repository](${base}tasks.md#4-worked-example-b1-procure-to-pay-week).\n`;
const rewire = (md: string) => md
  // Sections 4 onwards of tasks.md stay in the repository (see the cut above), so links into them go there.
  .replace(/\]\(tasks\.md#([4-9]-[^)]*)\)/g, `](${base}tasks.md#$1)`)
  .replace(/\]\((?:README|environment|tasks)\.md#([^)]+)\)/g, "](#$1)")
  .replace(/\]\(README\.md\)/g, "](#specification)")
  .replace(/\]\(environment\.md\)/g, "](#the-environment)")
  .replace(/\]\(tasks\.md\)/g, "](#the-tasks)");
const spec = renderMarkdown(rewire(readRepoFile("docs/process/README.md")), { stripFirstH1: true, linkBase: `${REPO}/blob/main/docs/process/` });
const env = renderMarkdown(rewire(readRepoFile("docs/process/environment.md")), { stripFirstH1: true, linkBase: `${REPO}/blob/main/docs/process/` });
const tasks = renderMarkdown(rewire(tasksPart), { stripFirstH1: true, linkBase: `${REPO}/blob/main/docs/process/` });
const toc = [
  { depth: 2, id: "implementation-status", text: "Implementation and evidence" },
  { depth: 2, id: "specification", text: "Specification" }, ...spec.toc.filter((t) => t.depth === 2).map((t) => ({ ...t, depth: 3 })),
  { depth: 2, id: "the-environment", text: "The environment" }, ...env.toc.filter((t) => t.depth === 2).map((t) => ({ ...t, depth: 3 })),
  { depth: 2, id: "the-tasks", text: "The tasks" }, ...tasks.toc.filter((t) => t.depth === 2).map((t) => ({ ...t, depth: 3 })),
];
const desc = "Working specification of the Business Bench process track, with implemented components, the published fixed-seed pilot, and planned capabilities distinguished.";
---
<Base title="Process track specification" description={desc} path="/process/spec" crumbs={[{ name: "Process track", path: "/process" }, { name: "Specification", path: "/process/spec" }]}>
  <p class="meta"><a href="/process">Process track</a><span class="sep">·</span>specification<span class="sep">·</span>rendered from <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/docs/process`} rel="noopener">docs/process</a></p>
  <h1>Process track specification</h1>
  <p class="lede">The track design, the ERP the agent operates, and the planned task catalogue. Read the design requirements alongside the implemented inventory and recorded campaign conditions below.</p>
  <nav slot="contents" class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><span class="toc-h">On this page</span>{toc.map((t) => <a href={`#${t.id}`} class={`d${t.depth}`}>{t.text}</a>)}</nav>
  <section aria-labelledby="implementation-status">
    <h2 id="implementation-status">Implementation and evidence</h2>
    <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
      <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Current status</th><th>What to consult</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Implemented environment and tasks</td><td>bb-erp, a multi-turn runner, validators, and {inventory.length} task packs. The runner currently uses local processes.</td><td><a href="/process#tasks">Task inventory</a>; <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/bench/process_run.py`} rel="noopener">runner</a>; <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/bench/validate_process.py`} rel="noopener">validator</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Published empirical evidence</td><td>{pilot.tasks.length} tasks, seed {pilot.seed}, {pilot.repetitions} repeated attempts per system. Fixed-seed repeatability under pilot conditions.</td><td><a href="/process#campaign">Campaign results and conditions</a>; <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/results/process/${PROCESS_PILOT}/provenance.json`} rel="noopener">provenance</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Design and planned coverage</td><td>The documents below describe the broader task catalogue, desired execution boundaries, and evaluation procedures. A requirement in this specification is not evidence of implementation or validation.</td><td><a href="/roadmap">Roadmap</a>; <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/STATUS.md`} rel="noopener">repository status</a>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p>An oracle pass establishes that a supplied policy can satisfy the declared tests; a targeted negative control demonstrates a specific rejection. Neither estimates agreement with practitioner acceptance, unseen-template performance, or production safety. Repeating seed {pilot.seed} is not the same experiment as testing additional seeds.</p>
    <p>For commands that separate task validation, new paid runs, and published-accounting checks, use <a href="/reproduce#process-experiment">the reproduction guide</a>. When the design and implementation differ, report the code version and actual conditions used, rather than treating the design as an execution record.</p>
  </section>
  <article class="prose"><h2 id="specification" style="margin-top:0">Specification</h2><div set:html={spec.html} /></article>
  <article class="prose"><h2 id="the-environment">The environment</h2><div set:html={env.html} /></article>
  <article class="prose" style="max-width:none"><h2 id="the-tasks">The tasks</h2><div set:html={tasks.html} /></article>
</Base>
